## Temporal Recurrence and Pressure / Release

| Window | Pink-Pepper current state | Material-level cause | Required recognition |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0-5 min | effervescent berry-pepper voltage | exact Pink Pepper + grapefruit/lemon + aldehydic/mineral points | Pink Pepper first; obvious athletic movement second |
| 30 min | pink aromatic current | exact Pink Pepper through linalyl/lavender cloth and Hedione/Hexyl release | still pepper-led; no shower-gel lavender |
| 2 h | peppered cedar current | cedar/Iso E contour meets AIMI, Clearwood, vetiver, and Sandalore | same subject becomes darker and smoother |
| 6 h | dry pepper-root fabric | vetiver, tiny patchouli shadow, Cashmeran, Romandolide | recognizable recurrence, not only performance materials |
| 24 h | warm woody-spice residue | sandalwood pair, cedar, quiet matrix, one musk | subject echo survives without harsh amberwood |

**Pressure module:** Pink Pepper + Dihydromyrcenol + grapefruit/lemon + tiny metallic points + restrained Ambrofix/Amber Xtreme rear edge.  
**Release module:** Hedione + Hexyl Salicylate + yielding Sandalore/Ebanol + quiet Benzyl Benzoate mass.  
**Expected collision:** 5-120 minutes.  
**Hedonic hypothesis:** the re-smell moment is the conversion of cold rosy-pepper voltage into a warm, polished cedar-sandal current. This remains **NOT TESTED**.

## Takeover Exclusions

| Exclusion | Observable endpoint | Stop rule |
|---|---|---|
| lavender/shower-gel takeover | lavender, soap, deodorant, or generic blue is named before Pink Pepper | reject regardless of liking |
| ambrox/Iso E wall | dry mineral wood is the only object from 30 min onward; fatigue or anosmia collapse rises | reduce rear-pressure module; do not add another amberwood |
| aquatic takeover | calone/melon/sea spray, loud ozone, or apple-blossom muguet is reported | reject mineral-air module at tested dose |
| literal rose/powder | rose, lychee, plum, lipstick, violet makeup, or cosmetic powder displaces pepper | remove trace lens/add-back before increasing Pink Pepper |
| sweet Parfum drift | vanilla, tonka dessert, balsam, cream, or syrup becomes the base identity | reject; no sweet rescue |
| donor-signature drift | saffron leather, smoky oak, incense, or recognizable Bleu/Prada reconstruction | reject even if preferred |
| static heaviness | intense but not athletic; no directional opening-to-heart motion | reject or lower warm-interior/rear module |

